    <string name="tuto_ride_summary">The riding map: follow the active track, see the next turns and record the ride.</string>
    <string name="tuto_follow">Following a track</string>
    <string name="tuto_follow_1">The active track (ticked circle in the Library) is drawn on the map, with chevrons in the riding direction and signs on steep slopes.</string>
    <string name="tuto_follow_2">The side banner announces the next turn with a countdown; the screen flashes in the last 100 meters.</string>
    <string name="tuto_follow_3">If you stray more than 30 m, the “Off track” chip appears; after 30 s it shows the distance back to the track.</string>
    <string name="tuto_follow_4">Beyond 100 m for 2 s, the “Rejoin the track” banner guides you by road to the nearest point of the track ahead, path in blue dots.</string>
    <string name="tuto_follow_5">Tap the track to “Resume the track here”: route to the tapped point, to confirm.</string>
    <string name="tuto_record">Recording the ride</string>
    <string name="tuto_record_1">When following starts, the app offers to record the ride. Recommended, but you can decline.</string>
    <string name="tuto_record_2">The button above the speedometer starts, pauses or resumes recording.</string>
    <string name="tuto_record_3">Recording continues in other tabs, with the screen off or in another app: a “GPXroad” notification shows it.</string>
    <string name="tuto_record_4">Tap the speedometer for stats, then “Finish the ride” to save it in the Library or delete it.</string>
    <string name="tuto_controls">Controls</string>
    <string name="tuto_controls_1">+ and − zoom; “Recenter” (top of the column) brings the map back to your position. Long-press the map: “Go here”.</string>
    <string name="tuto_controls_2">Pause suspends guidance (long-press: stop it). The track and recording stay active.</string>
    <string name="tuto_controls_3">“Blocked” reports an impassable path and offers a detour by road, by trail or direct.</string>
    <string name="tuto_goto_summary">Go to an address or place, outside any track.</string>
    <string name="tuto_goto_search">Finding a destination</string>
    <string name="tuto_goto_1">Type an address or place, then choose a profile: Route (roads), Trail or Mixed.</string>
    <string name="tuto_goto_2">Home and Work in one tap: long-press a result to set them.</string>
    <string name="tuto_goto_3">Your last searches are offered when the field is empty.</string>
    <string name="tuto_goto_during">During guidance</string>
    <string name="tuto_goto_4">With Valhalla set up (Settings), the Route profile gives detailed guidance: maneuvers, voice, recalculation if you stray. Otherwise, simple guidance to the destination.</string>
    <string name="tuto_goto_5">Only one guidance at a time: the track stays visible but its Road Book pauses. Tap the track or “Back to the track” to return.</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_summary">The active track as a list of directions, like a paper rally road book.</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_modes">Two reading modes</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_1">GPS assisted: the next item large, with the distance counting down, then the list of what follows.</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_2">Classic roadbook: the whole list with partial and total distances, like on paper.</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_3">The next item is the nearest, turn or landmark; a scenery landmark (church, bridge…) closely followed by a turn leaves the big card to the turn.</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_4">If you stray, the Road Book guides you by road back to the track, always to a point ahead of you.</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_roundabouts">Roundabouts and landmarks</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_5">The roundabout is drawn with all its roads, your path in color; the exit number is shown only when certain, with the exit road.</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_6">Only what can be seen from the road is shown: signs, bridges, churches, stations, village entrances. Categories in Settings.</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_other">Other actions</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_7">The track name at the top opens the Library; “PDF” exports a printable road book; tapping an item shows it on the Ride map.</string>
    <string name="tuto_rb_8">Paper colors by day, dark at night (based on the sun), or your choice in Settings.</string>
    <string name="tuto_lib_summary">Your GPX tracks: import, choose the active track, organize, share.</string>
    <string name="tuto_lib_tracks">Tracks</string>
    <string name="tuto_lib_1">“Import a GPX” adds a file (or open it from another app with GPXroad).</string>
    <string name="tuto_lib_2">The circle on the left makes a track active: Ride and Road Book follow it.</string>
    <string name="tuto_lib_3">A tap opens its sheet: stats, offline map, sharing, direction, renaming, folder, deletion.</string>
    <string name="tuto_lib_4">“New folder” then “Move” to organize; deleting a folder never deletes its tracks.</string>
    <string name="tuto_lib_5">A ride in progress is saved regularly; if the app closes, recover it in “Unsaved rides”.</string>
    <string name="tuto_set_summary">All settings apply immediately.</string>
    <string name="tuto_set_main">Main settings</string>
    <string name="tuto_set_1">Language: automatic (phone language) or forced.</string>
    <string name="tuto_set_2">Ride: track color and thickness, chevrons, controls side, slopes, flash, screen on.</string>
    <string name="tuto_set_4">Road Book: palette, turn sensitivity, landmark categories; recording: density and backups.</string>
    <string name="tuto_set_5">Advanced: Valhalla routing and Overpass server (optional), blocked points server.</string>
